  "query": "What is the speed of sound in air at 20 °C, in metres per second?",
  "answer": "In dry air at 20 °C, sound travels at about 343 m/s, which is roughly 1,235 km/h or 1,125 ft/s [1][2][3]. More exact values are 343.2 m/s [2] and, in one reference table, 343.37 m/s [1]. The speed depends mostly on temperature. It is about 331 m/s at 0 °C and rises by roughly 0.6 m/s for each degree Celsius [3]. Humid air carries sound slightly faster than dry air, because water vapour makes the air less dense.",
